        "original_id": "d8c4e2df-c845-5228-8ac7-a2b877abd255",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Spencer, Nick Cannon, Quincy Jones, Bill Clinton, Jamie Foxx, Wayans family\n- Shows: Wild 'N Out, All That, The Nick Cannon Show, America's Got Talent, Vibe\n- Topics: television hosting, writing, entertainment careers\n\nFacts:\n- In August 1997, the talk show Vibe premiered with Quincy Jones as producer, Chris Spencer as host, and President Bill Clinton as the first-episode guest.\n- Nick Cannon was born on October 8, 1980.\n- On television, Nick Cannon began as a teenager on All That.\n- Nick Cannon later hosted The Nick Cannon Show, Wild 'N Out, and America's Got Talent.\n- Nick Cannon is an American rapper, actor, comedian, director, screenwriter, film producer, entrepreneur, record producer, and radio and television personality.\n- Chris Spencer worked as a writer on projects with the Wayans family and Jamie Foxx.\n- Chris Spencer significantly helped Nick Cannon create MTV's Wild 'N Out.",
